       "type": "text",
       "text": "I entered the order as ORD-0001: amlodipine 50 mg by mouth once daily.\n\nI added a note to the order. It says the dose is above the usual 10 mg/day maximum and that you confirmed it's intentional. It also records that a specialist reportedly recommended it after standard dosing failed. It asks pharmacy to verify the dose and nursing to monitor BP and HR closely.\n\nPharmacy may call you to confirm the dose, since it's well above the labeled maximum. Monitoring for hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema is also worth planning for."
